"""English account and PayPal notices, corresponding to the Korean notices."""
from html import escape


def page(c, kind):
    contact = f'<a href="mailto:{escape(c.seller_email, quote=True)}">{escape(c.seller_email)}</a>'
    seller = "".join(f"<p>{label}: {escape(value)}</p>" for label, value in (
        ("Legal business name", c.seller_name), ("Representative", c.seller_representative),
        ("Business registration", c.seller_registration), ("Online sales registration", c.seller_sales_registration),
        ("Address", c.seller_address), ("Phone", c.seller_phone), ("Email", c.seller_email)) if value)
    sections = {
        "terms": ("Terms and refunds", f"""
<h2>The service</h2><p>Smooth Player plays videos you own or are authorized to access. A license provides continued access to supported smooth playback features. Movies, television programs, YouTube content and third-party subscriptions are not included. Performance and compatibility depend on the video and device. Try the app before buying; a specific frame rate or quality is not guaranteed.</p>
<h2>PayPal purchases</h2><p>PayPal prices are shown in US dollars (USD) before approval. Lifetime access is a single payment with no automatic renewal. A one-year license lasts 12 calendar months from the confirmed payment and does not renew automatically. The final product, price and terms appear at checkout. Lifetime access removes the smooth playback trial limit in a valid account and supported app; it does not include separately released future products or a promise to support every future device.</p>
<p>PayPal handles payment approval, payment methods and refunds on its own website. We do not receive your PayPal password or full card number. Review any exchange rate and conversion fees shown by PayPal or your payment provider before approval. Domestic transfers between Korean PayPal accounts are not supported. A Sandbox checkout is a test and does not charge real money or activate a production license.</p>
<h2>Other payment providers</h2><p>Toss Payments offers, when enabled, a monthly subscription at KRW {c.monthly_price:,}, a yearly subscription at KRW {c.yearly_price:,}, or lifetime access at KRW {c.lifetime_price:,}, including VAT. These are separate from PayPal's non-renewing products. Toss monthly and yearly subscriptions renew on the corresponding date, or the last day of that month if the date does not exist. Cancel automatic renewal from the Korean account page before the next payment; paid access remains through the paid period. Uninstalling the app does not cancel a subscription. An agreed recurring price is not increased automatically.</p>
<p>Apple and Google purchases follow their store policies. Linking an existing store purchase requires a supported app and successful server verification. A web purchase is not a promise of immediate compatibility with every existing app version on every platform.</p>
<h2>License activation and access</h2><p>After the server verifies payment, the license belongs to the email account used for checkout. Sign in with that same email in the app and refresh your license. An internet connection is required to verify access. Temporary offline access is limited to 24 hours since the last verification and never beyond a fixed-term license's expiry. Purchases are not transferred automatically to another account.</p>
<p>A valid complimentary code provides free lifetime access without creating a payment receipt or store purchase. Redeeming it stops that account's Toss renewal but does not refund existing payments. Cancel Apple or Google subscriptions in the corresponding store.</p>
<h2>Cancellation and refunds</h2><p>You may request withdrawal within the period provided by applicable law, generally seven days from receipt of the contract details or the start of supply. Restrictions for digital content already supplied apply only when the legal requirements, including prior disclosure and trial access, are met. Rights for defective service or service differing from its description or contract are not limited.</p>
<p>Contact {contact} with your purchase email, order number, payment date and reason. Do not send passwords or full card numbers. We review the transaction and applicable rights, process any required refund within the statutory period to the original payment method, and remove the refunded license after server confirmation. Payment-provider processing times vary. Cancelling future renewal is separate from refunding a past payment.</p>
<h2>Account deletion and changes</h2><p>You can delete your account from the app or Korean account page. This stops Toss renewal and account access, removes your email, and releases complimentary codes. Records needed for legal retention or preventing duplicate purchase linking are kept separately for the required period. Terms changes are published here with an effective version; adverse changes are notified as required by applicable law.</p>
"""),
        "privacy": ("Account and checkout privacy", f"""
<h2>Scope</h2><p>This notice covers email accounts, web payments and complimentary codes. App-specific notices are also available for <a href="https://smooth-player-support.vercel.app/privacy.html">Android</a> and <a href="https://smooth-player-support.vercel.app/ios/privacy.html">iOS</a>. Video, audio, subtitle files and local playlists are not uploaded to the account server. Supported signed-in apps can synchronize NAS connections and recent playback records.</p>
<h2>Account and payment data</h2><p>We process email addresses, random account identifiers, account creation times, verification-code hashes, expiry times and hashed login sessions. Temporary hashed IP/email identifiers and request counts help prevent abuse. Hosting providers may process operational request logs such as IP addresses and timestamps.</p>
<p>Purchase records include order identifiers, products, amounts, currency, payment status and time, provider transaction identifiers and the agreed terms version. Recurring billing identifiers are encrypted. We do not receive or store full card numbers, CVCs or card passwords. Complimentary codes are stored as verification hashes with account identifiers and redemption dates, not as plaintext codes. Requested store-purchase linking uses store transaction verification information.</p>
<h2>Optional Google or Apple sign-in</h2><p>The selected provider authenticates you and supplies an account identifier and verified email, including an Apple relay email when selected. We never receive those providers' passwords. Sign in to an existing email account before linking a provider to keep the same purchases and NAS data. Login verification state and security cookies last at most ten minutes; cookies are removed when authentication completes. Provider privacy policies also apply.</p>
<p>Linked identifiers are removed upon account deletion. Revocation tokens are encrypted and deleted after successful provider revocation; temporary failures are retried. A hash preventing reuse of a login started before deletion can be retained for up to one day.</p>
<h2>Optional playback synchronization</h2><p>NAS synchronization includes FTP/SMB host, port, share, starting path, encoding, username, password and domain; file names, paths, sizes, modification times, playback times and positions; and hidden NAS folder paths. Data travels over TLS and is encrypted in the database. The server does not connect to your NAS or retrieve videos. Public YouTube video IDs, titles and playback history can sync between supported devices; expiring download URLs do not.</p>
<p>Folder-lock PINs, local file/folder lists and preview images do not sync. Devices use operating-system secure storage for credentials and encrypted account caches for restoration and conflicts.</p>
<h2>Providers and international processing</h2><p>PayPal processes approvals, payments and refunds. This integration sends PayPal the product description, order identifier, amount, currency and merchant identifier, and verifies payment/refund identifiers and status. It does not send customer email, videos or NAS data to PayPal. Information collected by PayPal on its own website is governed by <a href="https://www.paypal.com/kr/legalhub/paypal/privacy-full">PayPal's privacy notice</a>.</p>
<p>Toss Payments handles its card authentication, payments, refunds and recurring charges. Vercel Inc. hosts the website and API; Neon, a Databricks service, operates the database; Resend (Plus Five Five, Inc.) sends verification emails. The main API and database region is Singapore. These US-based providers' support and operations, and Resend's email processing, may involve processing in the United States or other countries. Necessary data is transferred over encrypted connections to perform the service; email delivery includes the recipient email and verification message.</p>
<p>See the provider notices for <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel</a>, <a href="https://neon.com/privacy-policy">Neon</a> and <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy">Resend</a>. Limited operational logs and backups follow their contracts and retention policies. Contact {contact} about international processing or to object. Features requiring that processing may then be unavailable; local basic playback and store purchases follow their separate policies.</p>
<h2>Retention and deletion</h2><p>Email is retained while the account is active and removed on deletion. Verification codes expire after ten minutes; expired authentication, session and rate-limit records are periodically removed. Browser login tokens use tab session storage; apps use protected operating-system storage.</p>
<p>Complimentary-code records and server-side NAS/YouTube synchronization data are removed on account deletion. Deleting individual synced items propagates on the next synchronization; content-free deletion markers may remain while the account exists to prevent old devices restoring deleted items. Signing out hides that account's NAS list but keeps an encrypted local cache for later sign-in.</p>
<p>Under Korean electronic-commerce retention requirements, contract/withdrawal and payment/supply records are retained for five years, consumer complaint/dispute records for three years, and advertising records for six months. Purchase attribution needed to maintain a lifetime license remains while the service is used. After deletion, required transaction records are separated under an identifier without email, then destroyed after their retention period. Electronic records are deleted so they cannot be recovered.</p>
<h2>Your rights and security</h2><p>You can inspect licenses and subscriptions or delete your account after signing in. Request access, correction, deletion or restriction of processing at {contact}; we verify identity and respond under applicable law. Required legal retention may limit immediate deletion. Safeguards include encrypted transport, hashed authentication tokens, encrypted recurring-payment identifiers, restricted server secrets and signed license verification. This website uses no advertising trackers.</p>
<p>Privacy contact: {escape(c.seller_name)} customer support, {contact}, {escape(c.seller_phone)}. Korean privacy reporting and mediation: 118 and 1833-6972.</p>
"""),
        "support": ("Support and license setup", f"""
<h2>Before buying</h2><p>The Mac app requires Apple Silicon (M1 or later) and macOS 15 or later. Try smooth playback with your own authorized videos before buying. Support depends on input format, dynamic range, device and app version. Windows has a separate distribution and system requirements. Mobile purchase linking depends on the supported app version and server store-verification configuration.</p>
<h2>Activate a license</h2><ol><li>Sign in by email in the app's Account panel.</li><li>Sign in to this website with that same email and choose a license.</li><li>Approve payment on PayPal, return here, then refresh your license in the app.</li></ol><p>Sandbox purchases work only with a separate test build. They do not activate production apps. If a payment remains pending, use Check payment; do not start a second purchase.</p>
<h2>Renewals and refunds</h2><p>PayPal lifetime and one-year licenses do not renew automatically. Toss subscriptions can be cancelled from the Korean account page. Apple and Google subscriptions must be cancelled in the respective store. Cancellation of renewal does not automatically refund a previous payment.</p>
<h2>Contact us</h2><p>For refunds, send your purchase email, order number and payment date to {contact}. For technical issues, include the app version, operating system, device and the action that failed. Do not send private videos, NAS passwords, full card numbers or login codes. Phone: {escape(c.seller_phone)}.</p>
"""),
    }
    title, body = sections[kind]
    return f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{title} · Smooth Player</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"></head><body><main><a href="/en/">← Account and licenses</a><h1>{title}</h1><p class="muted">Effective version: {escape(c.terms_version)}</p><article>{body}</article><footer>{seller}<nav><a href="/privacy?lang=en">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms?lang=en">Terms and refunds</a> · <a href="/support?lang=en">Support</a></nav></footer></main></body></html>'
